WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
West Belfast.

2
00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:06.170
In Turf Lodge ward, 94.9 per
cent of residents are Catholic,

3
00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.090
or were brought up Catholic.

4
00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:12.910
In Shankill ward, 80.4 per cent
are Protestant and other Christian.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:19.110
Yet across the whole city, it's 48.7 per
cent Catholic and 36.4 per cent Protestant

6
00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:20.810
and other Christian.

7
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.070
Community barricades went up in 1969.

8
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:27.970
Paramilitary ceasefires came in 1994.

9
00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.490
So why does the city stay divided?

10
00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.610
Do people choose to live apart?

11
00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:34.430
Do walls keep them apart?

12
00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.850
Is housing cheaper?

13
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:38.270
Or is it no longer divided?

14
00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:40.770
In this mission, you'll
map Belfast's wards,

15
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:43.450
and find out what keeps them apart.

16
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:48.130
Then you'll test policies for living
together against the evidence on the ground.

17
00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.110
Your mission: explain why
Belfast stays divided.
